{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280513-virtue-and-momentum-in-hero","id":1280513,"title":"Virtue and Momentum in Hero","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-13T11:15:41-08:00","id":1280513,"title":"Virtue and Momentum in Hero","content":"In Origin, it\u2019s stated that a player may spend Momentum from the Momentum pool for any roll, as long as the other players agree. However, in Hero, there seems to be an unspoken assumption that Heroes can only spend Momentum in rolls specifically related to their pantheon virtues (or to power Knacks or Boons). For example, the write-up on the Virtuous condition seems to assume that you\u2019re spending Momentum on an action related to one of your Virtues (and if you\u2019re Virtuous, you get to add another die without spending a Momentum point).<br /> <br /> Am I reading this right? That Origin level characters can spend Momentum on any action (provided the other players agree), but Heroes can only spend Momentum on virtue-related actions? \u2014Jim Gardner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T12:58:43-08:00","id":1280536,"title":"","content":"That's actually a bit unclear. Near as I can figure, the difference is this:<br /> <br /> PCs, at any point, can spend 1 Momentum to add one die to any roll.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER! The Virtues Sidebar in Origin notes that if you spend Momentum in a roll that acts in accordance with one of your Virtues <b>adds a bonus die</b>. This could be made a bit more clear, but my takeaway is that if you spend a Momentum enhancing a roll that aligns with a Virtue, that one Momentum gives you <b>two</b> dice.<br /> <br /> The advantage of the Virtuous Condition is that the two-for-one thing applies all the time, but you can't go against your Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T15:24:23-08:00","id":1280776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280513-virtue-and-momentum-in-hero?p=1280536#post1280536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a bit unclear. Near as I can figure, the difference is this:<br /> <br /> PCs, at any point, can spend 1 Momentum to add one die to any roll.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER! The Virtues Sidebar in Origin notes that if you spend Momentum in a roll that acts in accordance with one of your Virtues <b>adds a bonus die</b>. This could be made a bit more clear, but my takeaway is that if you spend a Momentum enhancing a roll that aligns with a Virtue, that one Momentum gives you <b>two</b> dice.<br /> <br /> The advantage of the Virtuous Condition is that the two-for-one thing applies all the time, but you can't go against your Virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. You can still spend Momentum at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T16:16:47-08:00","id":1280788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280513-virtue-and-momentum-in-hero?p=1280776#post1280776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is correct. You can still spend Momentum at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed this is a common source of confusion, you may want to make it clearer in Hero that you can still spend Momentum at any point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}